</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S5.F7.fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:112.1pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2606.14164v1/props-oracle-functionalies.svg" id="S5.F7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:155/153;" width="155" height="153"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F7.fig3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S5.F7.fig3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Distribution of functional and non-functional fuzz oracles.
</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="S5.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Proportions of fuzz oracles the <span id="S5.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1,068</span> OSS-Fuzz drivers.</span><span id="acmlabel7" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">Statistics of fuzz oracles in \nossfuzzdrivers{} \ossfuzz{} drivers.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span><span id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RQ2:</span> Evaluation of LLM-based MRG</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="242.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 242.62" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,242.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.12 L 0 237.5 C 0 240.33 2.29 242.62 5.12 242.62 L 472.26 242.62 C 475.08 242.62 477.38 240.33 477.38 237.5 L 477.38 5.12 C 477.38 2.29 475.08 0 472.26 0 L 5.12 0 C 2.29 0 0 2.29 0 5.12 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#ECECEC;" fill="#ECECEC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.66 5.12 L 1.66 237.5 C 1.66 239.41 3.21 240.96 5.12 240.96 L 472.26 240.96 C 474.17 240.96 475.72 239.41 475.72 237.5 L 475.72 5.12 C 475.72 3.21 474.17 1.66 472.26 1.66 L 5.12 1.66 C 3.21 1.66 1.66 3.21 1.66 5.12 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.2 8.58)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.46em;--ltx-fo-height:16.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="225.47" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 225.47)" width="462.99"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S5.SS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.46em;">
<span id="S5.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Finding 2:<span id="S5.SS2.p1.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> 
MetaFOE generates 272–485 MRs for the 10 projects, with an overall applicable proportion of 77.3%.
These results demonstrate the feasibility of LLM-based MRG with promising effectiveness.
The applicable proportion of generated MRs is weakly negatively correlated with the LoC of the projects, with a Pearson Correlation Coefficient of -0.38.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.1. </span>Subjects of MFOE Experiments</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The columns 1–3 of <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2.2. MRG Statistics ‣ 5.2. RQ2: Evaluation of LLM-based MRG ‣ 5. Results ‣ Investigating Metamorphic Fuzz Oracle Enhancement via Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a> present the projects and drivers selected for the MFOE experiments.
Specifically, we experiment with 10 projects from OSS-Fuzz, and select one representative driver for each project.
These projects are widely used in fuzzing research, strengthening the validity of our study <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolff et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">5.2.2. </span>MRG Statistics</h4>

<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The columns 4–6 of <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.2.2. MRG Statistics ‣ 5.2. RQ2: Evaluation of LLM-based MRG ‣ 5. Results ‣ Investigating Metamorphic Fuzz Oracle Enhancement via Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a> show the MRG results obtained in each subject, where the table heads #R, #UR, and #AR denote the counts of generated, unique, and applicable MRs; the last row presents the totals.
We report the counts for #R and #UR, and the counts and proportions for #AR.
The applicable proportion (AP) is calculated as <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\text{\#AR}}{\text{\#R}}\times 100\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mtext>#AR</mtext><mtext>#R</mtext></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\text{\#AR}}{\text{\#R}}\times 100\%</annotation></semantics></math>, which is shown in the table with smaller fonts.
As shown, MetaFOE generates 272–485 MRs for the 10 subjects, with an overall AP of 77.3%.
These results demonstrate the feasibility of LLM-based MRG, with a reasonably high AP exceeding 70%.
AP varies across subjects (67.8%–90.0%), suggesting that the generation of applicable MRs depends on the characteristics of the project under test.
To further investigate this dependency, we compute the Pearson correlation coefficient (PCC) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen et al., 2009</a>)</cite> between AP and the lines of code (LoC) of the projects (reported in <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.3.1. FOI Statistics ‣ 5.3. RQ3: Evaluation of LLM-based FOI ‣ 5. Results ‣ Investigating Metamorphic Fuzz Oracle Enhancement via Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a>).
The PCC is -0.38, indicating a weak negative correlation between AP and LoC.
This result is somewhat counterintuitive, as larger projects are expected to contain more constraints and thus should yield more MRs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1. </span>Experimental subjects and MFOE results for each project.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T1.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">ID</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Project</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Driver</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#R</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#UR</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#AR</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#D</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#CD</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.1.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">#VD</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">S01</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rapidjson</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">fuzzer</span></td>
